--- !u!1001 &1742570478
PrefabInstance:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  serializedVersion: 2
  m_Modification:
    m_TransformParent: {fileID: 1658452411}
    m_Modifications:
    - target: {fileID: 585395312865148023, guid: d3c71176f32c1274b929f3a88695a795,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: initialText
      value: '<size=40><b>CentComm Notice</b></size>                                                    
        __________________________________

        This is Barry Newheart from Customer
        Support, following up with your raised item regarding to the quote "SERIOUS
        Evacuation Shuttle Safety Violation".

        I''m afraid to once again
        inform you that the Evacuation Shuttle is performing correctly, the shuttlebombing
        is to do with the shuttle going off the docking position relative to the
        original Master Design. I must stress that this Design cannot be updated
        to reflect the current upper docking area due to shuttlebombing ruining any
        newer alterations.

        If you would like to minimise damage to the station
        upon evacuation, it is strongly recommended that you disassemble the upper
        corridor prior to the shuttle''s arrival.

        Regards,

        Barry'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 8692691054828270594, guid: d3c71176f32c1274b929f3a88695a795,
        type: 3}
